IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: ss 19, 20 and 20A -- applying to incorporate a company, its registration and notice of incorporation, what incorporation does,
-- who the first members are, the Registrar's power and duty to refuse registration, the appeal to the Minister, and the minimum of one member. Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- This module supplies the keel's seam for s 19 (the document is the constitution of the company registered with the Registrar under section 19, as amended from time to time).
-- The Registrar and the Minister appear only as holders of powers and duties over the applicant or the company; there is no seat for them.
--
-- Answers. `JUST TRUE` is yes; `JUST FALSE` is the text saying no in its own words; `NOTHING` is "the text does not say".
-- "Upon receipt", "On the registration", "On and from" and "where the Registrar is satisfied" are "when" gates: unmet, a duty or a deeming answers `JUST FALSE`
-- (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-H-S1 for a "may"). Periods are counted only by sg-periods.l4 (fork line F-H-P2).

§ `Section 19: registration and incorporation`

-- src:3659 | 19.—(1) A person desiring the incorporation of a company must —
-- src:3661 | (a) submit to the Registrar the constitution of the proposed
-- src:3662 | company and such other documents as may be prescribed;
-- src:3664 | (b) furnish the Registrar with the last day of the proposed
-- src:3665 | company’s first financial year and such other information
-- src:3666 | as may be prescribed; and
-- src:3668 | (c) pay the Registrar the prescribed fee.
@ref s 19(1) (src:3659-3668)
GIVEN `the person has submitted to the Registrar the constitution of the proposed company and such other documents as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has furnished the Registrar with the last day of the proposed company's first financial year and such other information as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has paid the Registrar the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(1) the person desiring the incorporation of the company has done everything the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the person has submitted to the Registrar the constitution of the proposed company and such other documents as may be prescribed` AND `the person has furnished the Registrar with the last day of the proposed company's first financial year and such other information as may be prescribed` AND `the person has paid the Registrar the prescribed fee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person desiring the incorporation of a company must -- (a) submit to the Registrar the constitution of the proposed company and such other documents as may be prescribed; (b) furnish the Registrar with the last day of the proposed company's first financial year and such other information as may be prescribed; and (c) pay the Registrar the prescribed fee" (a duty not fully met: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))

-- (2): "Either (a) a registered qualified individual ...; or (b) a person named in the constitution as a director or the secretary ..., must make a declaration".
-- Read as: a declaration from either one discharges the duty (fork line F-H-D3 in NOTES.md).
-- src:3672 | (2) Either —
-- src:3674 | (a) a registered qualified individual engaged in the formation
-- src:3675 | of the proposed company; or
-- src:3677 | (b) a person named in the constitution as a director or the
-- src:3678 | secretary of the proposed company,
-- src:3680 | must make a declaration to the Registrar that —
-- src:3682 | (c) all of the requirements of this Act relating to the formation
-- src:3683 | of the company have been complied with; and
-- src:3685 | (d) he or she has verified the identities of the subscribers to the
-- src:3686 | constitution, and of the persons named in the constitution
-- src:3687 | as officers of the proposed company,
-- src:3689 | and the Registrar may accept such declaration as sufficient evidence
-- src:3690 | of those matters.
@ref s 19(2) (src:3672-3690)
GIVEN `the person is a registered qualified individual engaged in the formation of the proposed company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is named in the constitution as a director or the secretary of the proposed company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(2) the person is one of those who may make the declaration to the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `the person is a registered qualified individual engaged in the formation of the proposed company` OR `the person is named in the constitution as a director or the secretary of the proposed company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Either (a) a registered qualified individual engaged in the formation of the proposed company; or (b) a person named in the constitution as a director or the secretary of the proposed company"; the text says nothing of anyone else

-- src:3672 | (2) Either —
-- src:3674 | (a) a registered qualified individual engaged in the formation
-- src:3675 | of the proposed company; or
-- src:3677 | (b) a person named in the constitution as a director or the
-- src:3678 | secretary of the proposed company,
-- src:3680 | must make a declaration to the Registrar that —
-- src:3682 | (c) all of the requirements of this Act relating to the formation
-- src:3683 | of the company have been complied with; and
-- src:3685 | (d) he or she has verified the identities of the subscribers to the
-- src:3686 | constitution, and of the persons named in the constitution
-- src:3687 | as officers of the proposed company,
-- src:3689 | and the Registrar may accept such declaration as sufficient evidence
-- src:3690 | of those matters.
@ref s 19(2) (src:3672-3690)
GIVEN `the declaration was made to the Registrar by a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration states that all of the requirements of this Act relating to the formation of the company have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration states that the person has verified the identities of the subscribers to the constitution and of the persons named in the constitution as officers of the proposed company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(2) the declaration required by the subsection has been made to the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `the declaration was made to the Registrar by a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)` AND `the declaration states that all of the requirements of this Act relating to the formation of the company have been complied with` AND `the declaration states that the person has verified the identities of the subscribers to the constitution and of the persons named in the constitution as officers of the proposed company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must make a declaration to the Registrar that -- (c) all of the requirements of this Act relating to the formation of the company have been complied with; and (d) he or she has verified the identities of the subscribers to the constitution, and of the persons named in the constitution as officers of the proposed company" (a duty not fully met: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))

-- src:3689 | and the Registrar may accept such declaration as sufficient evidence
-- src:3690 | of those matters.
@ref s 19(2) (src:3689-3690)
GIVEN `the declaration is a declaration required by subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(2) the Registrar may accept the declaration as sufficient evidence of those matters` MEANS
    IF `the declaration is a declaration required by subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Registrar may accept such declaration as sufficient evidence of those matters"; the text says nothing of any other declaration

-- src:3694 | (3) Upon receipt of the documents, information and payment
-- src:3695 | referred to in subsection (1) and declaration mentioned in
-- src:3700 | subsection (2), the Registrar must, subject to this Act, register the
-- src:3701 | company by registering its constitution.
@ref s 19(3) (src:3694-3701)
GIVEN `the Registrar has received the documents, information and payment referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has received the declaration mentioned in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another provision of this Act, such as section 20, requires the Registrar not to register the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(3) the Registrar must register the company by registering its constitution` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has received the documents, information and payment referred to in subsection (1)` AND `the Registrar has received the declaration mentioned in subsection (2)` AND (NOT `another provision of this Act, such as section 20, requires the Registrar not to register the constitution`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon receipt of the documents, information and payment referred to in subsection (1) and declaration mentioned in subsection (2), the Registrar must, subject to this Act, register the company by registering its constitution" (a duty whose "upon" gate is unmet, or that yields "subject to this Act": the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))

-- The seam the keel asks for (PLAN.md section 4, table A): "the document is the constitution of the company registered with the Registrar under section 19, as amended from time to time".
-- src:3694 | (3) Upon receipt of the documents, information and payment
-- src:3695 | referred to in subsection (1) and declaration mentioned in
-- src:3700 | subsection (2), the Registrar must, subject to this Act, register the
-- src:3701 | company by registering its constitution.
@ref s 19(3) (src:3694-3701)
GIVEN `the document is the constitution submitted to the Registrar under subsection (1)(a), or that constitution as amended from time to time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has registered the company by registering that constitution under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(3) the document is the constitution of the company registered with the Registrar under section 19, as amended from time to time` MEANS
    `the document is the constitution submitted to the Registrar under subsection (1)(a), or that constitution as amended from time to time` AND `the Registrar has registered the company by registering that constitution under subsection (3)`

-- src:3707 | (4) On the registration of the constitution the Registrar must issue in
-- src:3708 | the prescribed manner a notice of incorporation in the prescribed
-- src:3709 | form stating that the company is, on and from the date specified in the
-- src:3710 | notice, incorporated, and that the company is —
@ref s 19(4) (src:3707-3710)
GIVEN `the Registrar has registered the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(4) the Registrar must issue a notice of incorporation` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has registered the constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the registration of the constitution the Registrar must issue in the prescribed manner a notice of incorporation" (a duty whose "on" gate is unmet: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))

-- (4)(a) to (c) and the closing words: the notice states the kind of company "as the case may be", and "where applicable, that it is a private company".
-- A company limited both by shares and by guarantee is not one of (a) to (c): NOTHING (s 17(5) bars registering one).
-- src:3707 | (4) On the registration of the constitution the Registrar must issue in
-- src:3708 | the prescribed manner a notice of incorporation in the prescribed
-- src:3709 | form stating that the company is, on and from the date specified in the
-- src:3710 | notice, incorporated, and that the company is —
-- src:3712 | (a) a company limited by shares;
-- src:3714 | (b) a company limited by guarantee; or
-- src:3716 | (c) an unlimited company,
-- src:3718 | as the case may be, and where applicable, that it is a private company.
@ref s 19(4) (src:3707-3718)
GIVEN `the notice is issued in the prescribed manner and in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that the company is, on and from the date specified in the notice, incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of company the notice states` IS A `Liability of members`
      `the kind of company the company is` IS A `Liability of members`
      `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(4) the notice of incorporation states what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the kind of company the company is` EQUALS `limited by shares and by guarantee`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraphs (a) to (c) name a company limited by shares, a company limited by guarantee and an unlimited company; the text names no notice for a company limited both by shares and by guarantee
    ELSE (IF `the notice is issued in the prescribed manner and in the prescribed form` AND `the notice states that the company is, on and from the date specified in the notice, incorporated` AND `the kind of company the notice states` EQUALS `the kind of company the company is` AND ((NOT `the company is a private company`) OR `the notice states that the company is a private company`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must issue in the prescribed manner a notice of incorporation in the prescribed form stating that the company is, on and from the date specified in the notice, incorporated, and that the company is -- (a) a company limited by shares; (b) a company limited by guarantee; or (c) an unlimited company, as the case may be, and where applicable, that it is a private company" (a duty not fully met: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))

-- (5): "On and from the date of incorporation specified in the notice ... the subscribers to the constitution, together with such other persons as may from time to time become members of the company, are a body corporate by the name contained in the constitution capable immediately of exercising all the functions of an incorporated company and of suing and being sued and having perpetual succession with power to hold land".
-- src:3724 | (5) On and from the date of incorporation specified in the notice
-- src:3725 | issued under subsection (4) but subject to this Act, the subscribers to
-- src:3726 | the constitution, together with such other persons as may from time to
-- src:3727 | time become members of the company, are a body corporate by the
-- src:3728 | name contained in the constitution capable immediately of exercising
-- src:3729 | all the functions of an incorporated company and of suing and being
-- src:3730 | sued and having perpetual succession with power to hold land but
-- src:3731 | with such liability on the part of the members to contribute to the
-- src:3732 | assets of the company in the event of its being wound up as is
-- src:3733 | provided by this Act.
@ref s 19(5) (src:3724-3733)
GIVEN `the person is a subscriber to the constitution or another person who has become a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date of incorporation specified in the notice issued under subsection (4)` IS A DATE
      `another provision of this Act provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(5) the person is, with the other members, a body corporate capable of exercising all the functions of an incorporated company` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is a subscriber to the constitution or another person who has become a member of the company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "the subscribers to the constitution, together with such other persons as may from time to time become members of the company"; the text says nothing of anyone else
    ELSE (IF `another provision of this Act provides otherwise`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "but subject to this Act"; the provision that overrides is not in this subsection
          ELSE (IF `the date asked` AT LEAST `the date of incorporation specified in the notice issued under subsection (4)`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On and from the date of incorporation specified in the notice issued under subsection (4) ... are a body corporate" (a failed "on and from": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))

-- (5), last limb: "with such liability on the part of the members to contribute to the assets of the company in the event of its being wound up as is provided by this Act".
-- src:3731 | with such liability on the part of the members to contribute to the
-- src:3732 | assets of the company in the event of its being wound up as is
-- src:3733 | provided by this Act.
@ref s 19(5) (src:3731-3733)
GIVETH A MAYBE `Liability of members`
`s 19(5) the liability of the members to contribute to the assets of the company in the event of its being wound up` MEANS
    NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "with such liability ... as is provided by this Act"; the liability is stated elsewhere in the Act and the subsection names none

DECLARE `s 19(6) register` IS ONE OF
    `s 19(6)(a) the register of members kept by the public company under section 190`
    `s 19(6)(b) the electronic register of members kept by the Registrar under section 196A`
    `s 19(6) another register`

-- src:3739 | (6) The subscribers to the constitution are deemed to have agreed to
-- src:3740 | become members of the company and on the incorporation of the
-- src:3741 | company must be entered as members —
@ref s 19(6) (src:3739-3741)
GIVEN `the person is a subscriber to the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(6) the subscriber is deemed to have agreed to become a member of the company` MEANS
    IF `the person is a subscriber to the constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The subscribers to the constitution are deemed to have agreed to become members of the company"; the text says nothing of anyone else

-- src:3739 | (6) The subscribers to the constitution are deemed to have agreed to
-- src:3740 | become members of the company and on the incorporation of the
-- src:3741 | company must be entered as members —
-- src:3743 | (a) in the case of a public company — in the register of
-- src:3744 | members kept by the public company under section 190; or
-- src:3749 | (b) in the case of a private company — in the electronic
-- src:3750 | register of members kept by the Registrar under
-- src:3751 | section 196A.
@ref s 19(6) (src:3739-3751)
GIVEN `the company has been incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      register IS A `s 19(6) register`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(6) the subscriber must be entered as a member in the register` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company has been incorporated`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the incorporation of the company must be entered as members" (a duty whose "on" gate is unmet: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))
    ELSE (CONSIDER register
          WHEN `s 19(6)(a) the register of members kept by the public company under section 190` THEN (IF `the company is a public company` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) in the case of a public company"; the text names no register of this kind for any other company
          WHEN `s 19(6)(b) the electronic register of members kept by the Registrar under section 196A` THEN (IF `the company is a private company` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) in the case of a private company"; the text names no register of this kind for any other company
          OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraphs name two registers and say nothing of any other

-- src:3755 | (6A) Apart from the subscribers mentioned in subsection (6), every
-- src:3756 | other person who agrees to become a member of a company and
-- src:3757 | whose name is entered —
-- src:3759 | (a) in the case of a public company — in the register of
-- src:3760 | members kept by the public company under section 190; or
-- src:3762 | (b) in the case of a private company — in the electronic
-- src:3763 | register of members kept by the Registrar under
-- src:3764 | section 196A,
-- src:3766 | is a member of the company.
@ref s 19(6A) (src:3755-3766)
GIVEN `the person agrees to become a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a subscriber mentioned in subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's name is entered in the register of members kept by the public company under section 190` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's name is entered in the electronic register of members kept by the Registrar under section 196A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(6A) the person is a member of the company` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is a subscriber mentioned in subsection (6)`) AND `the person agrees to become a member of the company` AND ((`the company is a public company` AND `the person's name is entered in the register of members kept by the public company under section 190`) OR (`the company is a private company` AND `the person's name is entered in the electronic register of members kept by the Registrar under section 196A`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "every other person who agrees to become a member of a company and whose name is entered" in the register is a member; the text does not say that no one else is, and the other ways of becoming a member are not in this subsection

-- src:3770 | (7) Upon the application of a company and payment of the
-- src:3771 | prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company a
-- src:3772 | certificate of confirmation of incorporation.
@ref s 19(7) (src:3770-3772)
GIVEN `the company has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed fee has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(7) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate of confirmation of incorporation` MEANS
    IF `the company has applied` AND `the prescribed fee has been paid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon the application of a company and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate of confirmation of incorporation" (a duty whose "upon" gate is unmet: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))

§ `Section 20: power to refuse registration`

-- (1): a bar. JUST TRUE means the Registrar must not register. "unless the Registrar is satisfied" is an "unless": met, the answer is JUST FALSE.
-- src:3778 | 20.—(1) Without affecting the powers of the Registrar under
-- src:3779 | section 12(5), where a constitution is delivered for registration under
-- src:3780 | section 19, the Registrar must not register the constitution unless the
-- src:3781 | Registrar is satisfied that all the requirements of this Act in respect of
-- src:3782 | the registration and of all matters precedent and incidental thereto
-- src:3783 | have been complied with.
@ref s 20(1) (src:3778-3783)
GIVEN `a constitution is delivered for registration under section 19` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that all the requirements of this Act in respect of the registration and of all matters precedent and incidental thereto have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(1) the Registrar must not register the constitution` MEANS
    IF `a constitution is delivered for registration under section 19`
    THEN (IF `the Registrar is satisfied that all the requirements of this Act in respect of the registration and of all matters precedent and incidental thereto have been complied with`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Registrar must not register the constitution unless the Registrar is satisfied that all the requirements of this Act in respect of the registration and of all matters precedent and incidental thereto have been complied with" (an "unless", met)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a constitution is delivered for registration under section 19, the Registrar must not register the constitution" (a failed "where": the bar does not arise; the provision's own question)

-- src:3787 | (2) Despite anything in this Act or any rule of law, the Registrar
-- src:3788 | must refuse to register the constitution of a proposed company where
-- src:3789 | the Registrar is satisfied that —
-- src:3791 | (a) the proposed company is likely to be used for an unlawful
-- src:3792 | purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare
-- src:3793 | or good order in Singapore; or
-- src:3795 | (b) it would be contrary to the national security or interest for
-- src:3796 | the proposed company to be registered.
@ref s 20(2) (src:3787-3796)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the proposed company is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to the national security or interest for the proposed company to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the constitution of the proposed company` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is satisfied that the proposed company is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore` OR `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to the national security or interest for the proposed company to be registered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Registrar must refuse to register the constitution of a proposed company where the Registrar is satisfied that -- (a) ...; or (b) ..." (a duty whose "where" gate is unmet: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))

-- src:3803 | (3) Any person aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under
-- src:3804 | subsection (2) may, within 30 days of the date of the decision, appeal
-- src:3805 | to the Minister whose decision is final.
@ref s 20(3) (src:3803-3805)
GIVEN `the person is aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the decision` IS A DATE
      `the date the appeal is brought` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(3) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under subsection (2)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is that of "Any person aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under subsection (2)"; the text says nothing of anyone else
    ELSE (IF `the date the appeal is brought` AT LEAST `the date of the decision` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date of the decision` `the date the appeal is brought` 30 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, within 30 days of the date of the decision, appeal to the Minister" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); the day of the decision is in time, fork line F-H-P2)

-- src:3804 | subsection (2) may, within 30 days of the date of the decision, appeal
-- src:3805 | to the Minister whose decision is final.
@ref s 20(3) (src:3804-3805)
GIVEN `the decision is the Minister's decision on an appeal under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(3) the decision of the Minister on the appeal is final` MEANS
    IF `the decision is the Minister's decision on an appeal under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Minister whose decision is final" speaks of the decision on an appeal under this subsection; the text says nothing of any other decision

§ `Section 20A: minimum of one member`

-- src:3808 | 20A. A company must have at least one member.
@ref s 20A (src:3808)
GIVEN `the number of members of the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20A the company has at least one member` MEANS
    IF `the number of members of the company` AT LEAST 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must have at least one member" (a duty not met: the provision's own question; the text names no act and no time, so there is no regulative rule: NOTES.md, rules with no breach path)

§ `Regulative rules of ss 19 and 20: no time limit and no consequence the text states, so no breach path`

DECLARE `s 19 and 20 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 19(1)(a) submit to the Registrar the constitution of the proposed company and such other documents as may be prescribed`
    `s 19(1)(b) furnish the Registrar with the last day of the proposed company's first financial year and such other information as may be prescribed`
    `s 19(1)(c) pay the Registrar the prescribed fee`
    `s 19(2) make the declaration to the Registrar`
    `s 19(3) register the company by registering its constitution`
    `s 19(4) issue a notice of incorporation`
    `s 19(7) issue to the company a certificate of confirmation of incorporation`
    `s 20(1) register the constitution`
    `s 20(2) refuse to register the constitution`

-- src:3659 | 19.—(1) A person desiring the incorporation of a company must —
-- src:3661 | (a) submit to the Registrar the constitution of the proposed
-- src:3662 | company and such other documents as may be prescribed;
@ref s 19(1) (src:3659-3662)
GIVEN bearer IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 19 and 20 act`
`s 19(1)(a) rule: the person desiring incorporation's duty to submit the constitution and documents` MEANS
    PARTY bearer
    MUST `s 19(1)(a) submit to the Registrar the constitution of the proposed company and such other documents as may be prescribed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 19(1)(a) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY bearer BECAUSE "the person desiring the incorporation of a company did not submit the constitution and documents" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- src:3664 | (b) furnish the Registrar with the last day of the proposed
-- src:3665 | company’s first financial year and such other information
