    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 19(1)(b) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY bearer BECAUSE "the person desiring the incorporation of a company did not furnish the information" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- src:3668 | (c) pay the Registrar the prescribed fee.
