-- src:3672 | (2) Either —
-- src:3674 | (a) a registered qualified individual engaged in the formation
-- src:3675 | of the proposed company; or
-- src:3677 | (b) a person named in the constitution as a director or the
-- src:3678 | secretary of the proposed company,
-- src:3680 | must make a declaration to the Registrar that —
-- src:3682 | (c) all of the requirements of this Act relating to the formation
-- src:3683 | of the company have been complied with; and
-- src:3685 | (d) he or she has verified the identities of the subscribers to the
-- src:3686 | constitution, and of the persons named in the constitution
-- src:3687 | as officers of the proposed company,
-- src:3689 | and the Registrar may accept such declaration as sufficient evidence
-- src:3690 | of those matters.
@ref s 19(2) (src:3672-3690)
GIVEN bearer IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 19 and 20 act`
`s 19(2) rule: the duty to make the declaration to the Registrar` MEANS
    PARTY bearer
    MUST `s 19(2) make the declaration to the Registrar`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 19(2) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY bearer BECAUSE "the declaration required by section 19(2) was not made to the Registrar" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- src:3694 | (3) Upon receipt of the documents, information and payment
-- src:3695 | referred to in subsection (1) and declaration mentioned in
-- src:3700 | subsection (2), the Registrar must, subject to this Act, register the
-- src:3701 | company by registering its constitution.
